\begin_layout Subsection
Writing a VCF File
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Creating the VCF file and related files is accomplished by creating a directory
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

vcfr
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and typing:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
dir.create(
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

vcfr
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
library(mega2vcf)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Mega2VCF(
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

vcfr/vcf
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Mega2VCF takes an argument which is the prefix used on all the files it
 generates.
 We have chosen to make that a path that includes a directory so we keep
 all the generated data in one place.
 Mega2VCF is explained in greater depth in the Implementation Section [].
 The Mega2VCF function assumes the environment is contained in the global
 variable ENV.
 If this is not true supply an additional argument 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

envir
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 set to the environment you wish to use.
 Note, that this will create the traditional .vcf file as well as a .fam file
 (we do linkage), a .phe file (phenotypes) and a few others.
 Read the code to see how the file data is collected from the data frames.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Creating a GenABEL gwaa.data-class object
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This task is analogous to the previous exercise.
 Type:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
library(mega2genabel)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
seqsimgwaa = Mega2GenAbel(
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

MEGA
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The argument to Mega2GenAbel is a filename prefix that will be used to name
 the .tped/.fam files that are created as an intermediate read by GenABEL
 to produce a gwaa.data-class object.
 (See the Implementation Section [].) At this point, you can use any of the
 GenABEL provided functions on your data.
 Note: It would not make sense to take the original PLINK data on this tortuous
 path to get it into GenABEL.
 There are several data formats that Mega2 can read and transform into a
 database that are not directly readable by GenABEL.
 Any Mega2 databases can be read into R and then can be transformed to GenABEL
 analogous to this example with seqsimr.db.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Regression
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
VCF
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Its time to use the Mega2.BATCH.vcf file from the tar file .
