\begin_layout Standard
All this information is stored in a Mega2 database.
 The code in the provided functions illustrates how to assemble the correspondin
g data from the Mega2 data frames.
 The 
\emph on
mkVCFphe
\emph default
 is a bit subtle.
 The database contains a raw vector of 8 * the number of phenotypes byte
 (per person).
 The 8 bytes are either one double precision float number or two integers
 depending on the encoding in the 
\series bold
locus_table
\series default
 (quantitative or affective).
 
\emph on
readBin
\emph default
 is used for converting the raw bits in each reach 8 byte vector to the
 correct form.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection

\emph on
mega2genabel
\emph default
 Package Functions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The GenABEL CRAN package provides may functions for GWAS analysis.
 It also accepts GWAS data in several convenient formats.
 But Mega2 accepts input in more formats, notably, PLINK bed, VCF, IMPUTE2
 and even linkage.
 Thus 
\emph on
Mega2GenABEL
\emph default
 can be a bridge to easily convert your data into GenABEL format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
You must call the 
\emph on
read.Mega2DB 
\emph default
function from the 
\emph on
mega2
\emph default
 package and save the returned environment into ENV to load a Mega2 database.
 The function, 
\emph on
Mega2GenABEL
\emph default
, returns a gwaa.data-class object.
 It operates by writing the Mega2 data into one of the formats that GenABEL
 supports; in this case PLINK tped format.
 This requires a .fam file, a .phe file and a .tped file.
 The latter looks very much like a VCF .vcf file with entries on each row
 for the genotypes of each sample.
 (There are less fields before the genotype data and the genotype data show
 the real nucleotides rather than VCF REF/ALT field references.) 
\emph on
Mega2GenABEL
\emph default
 calls the GenABEL 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

glue
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 functions to process the a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

tped
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 file into a generic GenABEL 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

raw
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 format file and then it converts that raw format and a phenotypefile to
 a GenABEL gwaa.data-class object.
\end_layout

